; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MAZE  -  VM1 builds a maze, VM2 solves it   (two programs, one file)
; ==========================================================================
; Load this ONE file - it holds both programs: VM1 at $4000 and VM2 at $5000 -
; then cold-boot and press a key. VM1 carves a random 25 x 10 maze on screen (a
; depth-first backtracker, multitasking OFF so it has the whole CPU). Then it
; copies the grid into VM2's memory with $DC COPYBVMXVMY and triggers VM2 by
; writing 1 into VM2's RB with $D3 COPYVXY. VM2 solves it right-hand-on-the-wall:
; 'o' is the path, '.' the dead ends it backed out of.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing and reverse video (the walls) only.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/maze_verify.py, V0061.33, two-VM cold boot): three mazes, the first booted into DIRTY grid RAM and the second a RERUN from the memory the first left (no reload, as on the Elf2K) - it draws a NEW maze; each reads back off the screen as a PERFECT 25 x 10 maze equal to VM1's grid; VM2's copy has identical walls ($DC); the 'o' left on screen is exactly the start-to-exit path, '.' only off it, and the step and path counts match a Python right-hand walk. About 12-16 million 1802 instructions (~1.5 min at 3 MHz) + ~12 KB of output.
; The first build was HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.33), 2026-09-24. This build
; also rebuilds the grid at the start of every run (FILLMEM), so a rerun without
; reloading makes a new maze - that change is not yet run on hardware.
;
; VM1: 167 STELLAR commands.   VM2: 137 STELLAR commands.

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  VM1 ($4000): builds the maze, hands it over  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0C 00 34    LOADXI R12 0034                    The grid stride
; D 4009 11 0A 00 02    LOADXI R10 0002
; D 400D 11 03 08 00    LOADXI R3 0800
; D 4011 11 04 0C AB    LOADXI R4 0CAB
; D 4015 FB 34 58       FILLMEMXY R3..R4 'X'               A fresh grid: everything a sentinel ...
; D 4018 11 03 08 34    LOADXI R3 0834                     row 0
; D 401C 11 05 00 15    LOADXI R5 0015
; CLR:
; D 4020 23 00 34       COPYXY R3 -> R4
; D 4023 52 04 00 32    ADDXI R4 0032
; D 4027 FB 34 23       FILLMEMXY R3..R4 '#'               ... then each maze row solid, unvisited
; D 402A 52 03 00 34    ADDXI R3 0034
; D 402E 43 05          DECX R5
; D 4030 8C 05          TESTXZ R5
; D 4032 A1 00 20       IFFALSEI CLR
; D 4035 D0 11          SHAREVM on, read-only              VM2 may read us (the $DC source)
; WAIT2:
; D 4037 D1 22          TESTVM 2 RW                        Has VM2 opened itself read/write yet?
; D 4039 A1 00 37       IFFALSEI WAIT2                     Not yet - it needs one turn first
; D 403C 11 0E 06 00    LOADXI R14 0600
; D 4040 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4042 11 0E 06 44    LOADXI R14 0644
; D 4046 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; SEED:
; D 4048 C3             RAND                               Spin the generator until a key comes - every maze differs
; D 4049 CC             SERST
; D 404A A1 00 48       IFFALSEI SEED
; D 404D CB             SERIN                              and throw the key away
; D 404E C7 00          SETMULTI 00                        Multitasking OFF: VM2 is only waiting
; D 4050 11 0E 06 72    LOADXI R14 0672
; D 4054 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4056 11 0E 06 B4    LOADXI R14 06B4
; D 405A C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Reverse video: a space is a wall block
; D 405C 11 0D 00 03    LOADXI R13 0003
; D 4060 11 03 00 15    LOADXI R3 0015
; BLK:
; D 4064 11 0E 00 0F    LOADXI R14 000F
; D 4068 BD 01 BB       CALL POSXY
; D 406B 11 0E 07 C0    LOADXI R14 07C0
; D 406F C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       51 blocks
; D 4071 42 0D          INCX R13
; D 4073 43 03          DECX R3
; D 4075 8C 03          TESTXZ R3
; D 4077 A1 00 64       IFFALSEI BLK
; D 407A 11 0E 06 B9    LOADXI R14 06B9
; D 407E C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4080 11 07 00 20    LOADXI R7 0020                     R7 = the carving character, a normal-video space
; D 4084 11 0B 00 35    LOADXI R11 0035
; D 4088 BD 01 A3       CALL DRAW                          The way in (screen only)
; D 408B 11 0B 04 75    LOADXI R11 0475
; D 408F BD 01 A3       CALL DRAW                          The way out
; D 4092 11 06 00 69    LOADXI R6 0069
; D 4096 10 00 20       LOADAI 0020
; D 4099 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800                   Carve the first cell
; D 409D 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 40A0 BD 01 A3       CALL DRAW
; D 40A3 11 01 0D 00    LOADXI R1 0D00                     R1 = stack pointer
; D 40A7 3A 02 61       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R1)                push it
; D 40AA 52 01 00 02    ADDXI R1 0002
; LOOP:
; D 40AE 86 01 0D 00    TESTXI R1 0D00
; D 40B2 A0 01 76       IFTRUEI BUILT                      Stack empty: every cell visited
; D 40B5 23 00 18       COPYXY R1 -> R8
; D 40B8 53 08 00 02    SUBXI R8 0002
; D 40BC 39 02 82       COPYMXY M(R8) -> R2                R2 = current cell
; D 40BF 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000                     R5 = unvisited neighbours found
; D 40C3 11 09 0F 00    LOADXI R9 0F00
; D 40C7 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40CA 52 06 00 02    ADDXI R6 0002                      right
; D 40CE 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40D2 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40D5 A1 00 E1       IFFALSEI NB0
; D 40D8 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 40DB 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 40DF 42 05          INCX R5
; NB0:
; D 40E1 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40E4 53 06 00 02    SUBXI R6 0002                      left
; D 40E8 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40EC 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40EF A1 00 FB       IFFALSEI NB1
; D 40F2 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 40F5 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 40F9 42 05          INCX R5
; NB1:
; D 40FB 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40FE 52 06 00 68    ADDXI R6 0068                      down
; D 4102 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 4106 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 4109 A1 01 15       IFFALSEI NB2
; D 410C 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 410F 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 4113 42 05          INCX R5
; NB2:
; D 4115 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 4118 53 06 00 68    SUBXI R6 0068                      up
; D 411C 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 4120 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 4123 A1 01 2F       IFFALSEI NB3
; D 4126 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 4129 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 412D 42 05          INCX R5
; NB3:
; D 412F 8C 05          TESTXZ R5
; D 4131 A1 01 3B       IFFALSEI PICK
; D 4134 53 01 00 02    SUBXI R1 0002                      Dead end: pop
; D 4138 B0 00 AE       GAL LOOP
; PICK:
; D 413B C3             RAND                               A random one of them
; D 413C 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6
; D 413E 4D 65          DIVXY R6 / R5
; D 4140 27             COPYREMA
; D 4141 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8
; D 4143 50 88 08       ADDXYZ R8 + R8 -> R8               x2: a word each
; D 4146 52 08 0F 00    ADDXI R8 0F00
; D 414A 39 02 86       COPYMXY M(R8) -> R6                R6 = the chosen cell
; D 414D 50 26 08       ADDXYZ R2 + R6 -> R8
; D 4150 4D 8A          DIVXY R8 / R10
; D 4152 25             COPYMAA
; D 4153 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8                   R8 = the wall between = (cur + next) / 2
; D 4155 10 00 20       LOADAI 0020
; D 4158 2F 08 08 00    WRITEIDX R8 0800                   knock it down
; D 415C 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800                   and visit the cell
; D 4160 23 00 8B       COPYXY R8 -> R11
; D 4163 BD 01 A3       CALL DRAW
; D 4166 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 4169 BD 01 A3       CALL DRAW
; D 416C 3A 02 61       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R1)                push it
; D 416F 52 01 00 02    ADDXI R1 0002
; D 4173 B0 00 AE       GAL LOOP
; BUILT:
; D 4176 11 03 08 00    LOADXI R3 0800                     The grid is at the same place in both VMs
; D 417A 11 06 00 05    LOADXI R6 0005
; COPY:
; D 417E D3 21 33       COPYVXY save R3 -> VM2 R3          VM2's R3 = the same address, in VM2
; D 4181 DC 13 23 F0    COPYBVMXVMY VM1 R3 -> VM2 R3 F0    240 bytes, VM1 to VM2
; D 4185 52 03 00 F0    ADDXI R3 00F0
; D 4189 43 06          DECX R6
; D 418B 8C 06          TESTXZ R6
; D 418D A1 01 7E       IFFALSEI COPY
; D 4190 11 0B 00 01    LOADXI R11 0001
; D 4194 D3 21 BB       COPYVXY save RB -> VM2 RB          The trigger: VM2 is waiting for RB = 1
; D 4197 11 0E 06 BE    LOADXI R14 06BE
; D 419B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 419D C7 01          SETMULTI 01                        Multitasking back ON - VM2 takes over
; D 419F 00             HALT                               VM1 is done
; D 41A0 F0 00 00       BREAK
; DRAW:
; D 41A3 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12                    row + 1, column
; D 41A5 25             COPYMAA
; D 41A6 21 0D          COPYAX Acc -> R13
; D 41A8 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 41AC 27             COPYREMA
; D 41AD 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 41AF 52 0E 00 0F    ADDXI R14 000F
; D 41B3 BD 01 BB       CALL POSXY
; D 41B6 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 41B8 C9             SEROUT
; D 41B9 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 41BB CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B
; D 41BD CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['
; D 41BF 4D DF          DIVXY R13 / R15
; D 41C1 25             COPYMAA
; D 41C2 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41C5 C9             SEROUT
; D 41C6 27             COPYREMA
; D 41C7 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41CA C9             SEROUT
; D 41CB CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'
; D 41CD 4D EF          DIVXY R14 / R15
; D 41CF 25             COPYMAA
; D 41D0 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41D3 C9             SEROUT
; D 41D4 27             COPYREMA
; D 41D5 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41D8 C9             SEROUT
; D 41D9 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'
; D 41DB BE 00          RETURN

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  VM2 ($5000): solves it  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 5000 CD             START
; D 5001 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: VM1 sets it to 1 when the maze is ours
; D 5005 D0 12          SHAREVM on, read/write             VM1 may write our memory and registers
; D 5007 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 500B 11 0C 00 34    LOADXI R12 0034
; WAIT:
; D 500F 86 0B 00 01    TESTXI R11 0001
; D 5013 A1 00 0F       IFFALSEI WAIT                      Wait for the trigger
; D 5016 11 0E 06 00    LOADXI R14 0600
; D 501A C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 501C 11 05 04 41    LOADXI R5 0441                     R5 = the bottom-right cell
; D 5020 11 02 00 69    LOADXI R2 0069                     R2 = where we are
; D 5024 11 03 00 02    LOADXI R3 0002                     R3 = heading: 0 up 1 right 2 down 3 left
; D 5028 10 00 6F       LOADAI 006F
; D 502B 2F 02 08 00    WRITEIDX R2 0800
; D 502F 11 0A 00 6F    LOADXI R10 006F
; D 5033 23 00 2B       COPYXY R2 -> R11
; D 5036 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5039 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001                     R8 = path length (cells)
; D 503D 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000                     R9 = steps
; STEP:
; D 5041 87 25          TESTXY R2 = R5
; D 5043 A0 00 C3       IFTRUEI SOLVED
; D 5046 23 00 34       COPYXY R3 -> R4
; D 5049 42 04          INCX R4
; D 504B 86 04 00 04    TESTXI R4 0004
; D 504F A1 00 56       IFFALSEI TRY                       R4 = heading + 1: try RIGHT first
; D 5052 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; TRY:
; D 5056 BD 00 E8       CALL OFF                           R6 = the wall that way, R7 = the cell beyond
; D 5059 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 505D 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023
; D 5060 A1 00 71       IFFALSEI FOUND                     Open
; D 5063 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 5065 A1 00 6C       IFFALSEI TL                        Blocked: turn left one
; D 5068 11 04 00 04    LOADXI R4 0004
; TL:
; D 506C 43 04          DECX R4
; D 506E B0 00 56       GAL TRY
; FOUND:
; D 5071 42 09          INCX R9
; D 5073 2E 07 08 00    READIDX R7 0800
; D 5077 81 00 6F       TESTAI 006F
; D 507A A0 00 9D       IFTRUEI BACK                       Stepping back onto the path
; D 507D 10 00 6F       LOADAI 006F
; D 5080 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800
; D 5084 2F 07 08 00    WRITEIDX R7 0800
; D 5088 11 0A 00 6F    LOADXI R10 006F
; D 508C 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 508F BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5092 23 00 7B       COPYXY R7 -> R11
; D 5095 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5098 42 08          INCX R8
; D 509A B0 00 BA       GAL MOVED
; BACK:
; D 509D 10 00 2E       LOADAI 002E
; D 50A0 2F 02 08 00    WRITEIDX R2 0800
; D 50A4 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800
; D 50A8 11 0A 00 2E    LOADXI R10 002E
; D 50AC 23 00 2B       COPYXY R2 -> R11
; D 50AF BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 50B2 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 50B5 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 50B8 43 08          DECX R8
; MOVED:
; D 50BA 23 00 72       COPYXY R7 -> R2
; D 50BD 23 00 43       COPYXY R4 -> R3
; D 50C0 B0 00 41       GAL STEP
; SOLVED:
; D 50C3 23 00 87       COPYXY R8 -> R7                    Path length out of R8: PRNUM counts digits in R8
; D 50C6 11 0E 06 39    LOADXI R14 0639
; D 50CA C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50CC 23 00 94       COPYXY R9 -> R4
; D 50CF BD 01 5B       CALL PRNUM
; D 50D2 11 0E 06 51    LOADXI R14 0651
; D 50D6 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50D8 23 00 74       COPYXY R7 -> R4
; D 50DB BD 01 5B       CALL PRNUM
; D 50DE 11 0E 06 67    LOADXI R14 0667
; D 50E2 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50E4 00             HALT
; D 50E5 F0 00 00       BREAK
; OFF:
; D 50E8 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 50EB 86 04 00 00    TESTXI R4 0000
; D 50EF A0 01 07       IFTRUEI OU
; D 50F2 86 04 00 01    TESTXI R4 0001
; D 50F6 A0 01 0E       IFTRUEI OR
; D 50F9 86 04 00 02    TESTXI R4 0002
; D 50FD A0 01 15       IFTRUEI OD
; D 5100 53 06 00 01    SUBXI R6 0001                      left
; D 5104 B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OU:
; D 5107 53 06 00 34    SUBXI R6 0034
; D 510B B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OR:
; D 510E 52 06 00 01    ADDXI R6 0001
; D 5112 B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OD:
; D 5115 52 06 00 34    ADDXI R6 0034
; ON:
; D 5119 50 66 07       ADDXYZ R6 + R6 -> R7
; D 511C 51 72 07       SUBXYZ R7 - R2 -> R7               next = 2 x wall - here
; D 511F BE 00          RETURN
; DRAW:
; D 5121 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12                    row + 1, column
; D 5123 25             COPYMAA
; D 5124 21 0D          COPYAX Acc -> R13
; D 5126 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 512A 27             COPYREMA
; D 512B 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 512D 52 0E 00 0F    ADDXI R14 000F
; D 5131 BD 01 39       CALL POSXY
; D 5134 22 0A          COPYXA R10 -> Acc
; D 5136 C9             SEROUT
; D 5137 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 5139 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B
; D 513B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['
; D 513D 4D DF          DIVXY R13 / R15
; D 513F 25             COPYMAA
; D 5140 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5143 C9             SEROUT
; D 5144 27             COPYREMA
; D 5145 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5148 C9             SEROUT
; D 5149 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'
; D 514B 4D EF          DIVXY R14 / R15
; D 514D 25             COPYMAA
; D 514E 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5151 C9             SEROUT
; D 5152 27             COPYREMA
; D 5153 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5156 C9             SEROUT
; D 5157 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'
; D 5159 BE 00          RETURN
; PRNUM:
; D 515B 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; PN1:
; D 515F 4D 4F          DIVXY R4 / R15
; D 5161 27             COPYREMA
; D 5162 70 00          PUSHA Acc                          digits onto the stack
; D 5164 42 08          INCX R8
; D 5166 25             COPYMAA
; D 5167 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4
; D 5169 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 516B A1 01 5F       IFFALSEI PN1
; PN2:
; D 516E 71 00          POPA Acc
; D 5170 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5173 C9             SEROUT
; D 5174 43 08          DECX R8
; D 5176 8C 08          TESTXZ R8
; D 5178 A1 01 6E       IFFALSEI PN2
; D 517B BE 00          RETURN

